{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.rank_four_needs_calculus_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.rank_four_needs_calculus_five","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CalculusDimensionObstruction.lean#L177-L182","doc":"The rank-4 distribution the self-duality blocks need would come from a\n**five**-dimensional calculus, still odd and still contact — not from the\n4-dimensional bicovariant one, which by `no_calculus_has_both` is not contact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.woronowicz_gives_n_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.woronowicz_gives_n_one","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CalculusDimensionObstruction.lean#L172-L175","doc":"The declared calculus gives `n = 1`, hence `dim M = 3` — a third independent\nvote for the 3-dimensional reading, and the only one with no geometry in it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.calculusDim_eq_crDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.calculusDim_eq_crDim","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CalculusDimensionObstruction.lean#L166-L170","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.crDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.crDim","kind":"def","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CalculusDimensionObstruction.lean#L161-L164","doc":"**The dimension dictionary.**  Matching `rank(ker Θ) = d − 1` categorically\nagainst `2n` archimedeanly gives `d = 2n + 1`: the calculus dimension is the\nmanifold dimension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.contact_volume_is_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.contact_volume_is_top","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CalculusDimensionObstruction.lean#L153-L159","doc":"**`Θ ∧ dΘ` is a top form there.**  `Θ` has degree 1 and `dΘ` degree 2, so the\nwedge has degree 3 — which is the top degree of a 3-dimensional calculus, and\n`Ω³` is one-dimensional.  So the categorical volume form is a genuine volume\nform, constructed with no manifold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.woronowicz_form_dims","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.woronowicz_form_dims","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CalculusDimensionObstruction.lean#L148-L151","doc":"The exterior algebra of the Woronowicz 3-dimensional calculus: `1, 3, 3, 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.formDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.formDim","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CalculusDimensionObstruction.lean#L145-L146","doc":"The dimension of `Ω^k` for a calculus of dimension `d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.woronowicz_has_no_selfDuality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.woronowicz_has_no_selfDuality","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CalculusDimensionObstruction.lean#L142-L143","doc":"…and at `d = 3` the star sends `Ω²` to `Ω¹`, so `Ω^±` is not definable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.woronowicz_is_contact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.woronowicz_is_contact","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CalculusDimensionObstruction.lean#L136-L140","doc":"The Woronowicz left-covariant calculus: `d = 3`, distribution rank 2, odd —\ncontact, as `categorical-reeb-brings.md` builds it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.no_calculus_has_both","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.no_calculus_has_both","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CalculusDimensionObstruction.lean#L124-L134","doc":"**No differential calculus carries both.**  Self-duality needs `d = 4`;\ncontactness needs `d` odd; `4` is even.\n\nThis is the categorical form of the archimedean obstruction, and it needs no\nmanifold, no metric, and no resolution of the `S³` ambiguity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.selfDual_forces_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.selfDual_forces_four","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CalculusDimensionObstruction.lean#L117-L122","doc":"**Self-duality of 2-forms forces the calculus dimension to be 4.**  Same fact\nas `SelfDualityDegree.selfDual_two_forms_iff_dim_four`, restated for a calculus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.contact_forces_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.contact_forces_odd","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CalculusDimensionObstruction.lean#L110-L115","doc":"**Contactness forces the calculus dimension to be odd.**  `dΘ` restricted to\n`ker Θ` is alternating and non-degenerate, so `ker Θ` has even rank. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.starTarget","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.starTarget","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CalculusDimensionObstruction.lean#L107-L108","doc":"The degree the categorical Hodge star sends `Ω^k` to. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.distributionRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CalculusDimensionObstruction.distributionRank","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/CalculusDimensionObstruction.lean#L104-L105","doc":"The rank of `ker Θ` inside a calculus of dimension `d`: one less. ","signatureChunk":0}]}